  "body": "Activating the new SDK requires actual source coverage and a full image containing that SDK. This adds one command that reproduces the pinned compiler-selected source, independently checks the authenticated retained full image, and binds both findings into an inactive closed-loop execution assessment. The requested actual image/runtime/closed-loop work remains INCOMPLETE: no native/model/official-ORT execution was performed.\n\nFinal HEAD: 62089536a5a4b94565781d155ef9eed3d81228ba; implementation f038a6d68dbf703a82203f6eda2e88a40b47b43f; base feature/panda-adapter-sdk-v1 at 45df9244b4e212af3c5f18628ba7639608a0b4cd. This PR remains Draft and unmerged.\n\nActual findings:\n\n- SDKaa7e14e71f98b083faa60536ecf6b0a05e3996b4771d38e4a2ccfd43c0903088 has 270 selected literal lookups, 11 existing routes and 259 remaining names versus safe cap256. Seven prefix-prohibited names and four computed resolver sites remain unqualified. Empty compiled table/privateGLX+POSIX are current reconstructed source facts, not observed runtime branches or a complete original host-header/object-path certificate. No automatic allowlist or budget increase.\n- Authenticated retained image: 1,726,678,016 bytes, SHA256f69b8ece51bcc6911aaf118d5ea091ba4d6ace8418b480e408be5b9fd8cb2921; config/rootfs/authority and 44,232 installed entries checked as DATA ONLY. Python/MetaDrive are present, but installed libpandagl is oldf38e0734a5344eda9a11e3024695febf2cea0177aa80985b67ceef5837a088d7, not newaa7e. No image/library replacement, Docker load/build or Panda/GL import.\n- Native assessment is BLOCKED_NOT_EXECUTED. Exact original 2seeds\u00d72scenes\u00d712steps\u00d72independent runs at20Hz/8mps and official modelID/SHA are PLANNED metadata only. New mapped ABI/dispatch, early install/identity/allocation lifetimes, environment, driver/read freshness, authenticated process/window/producer/sink receipts and a fresh bounded canary contract remain required.\n\nValidation:\n\n- 23 focused tests pass; full suite 1526 tests / 1519 pass / 7 skipped (118.442s).\n- Real CPU preprocessing excludes inactive branches; wrong-origin markers, changed compiler flags, lookup cap256/257, unsafe/computed names, forged routes, old/wrong-path/duplicate SDK inventory and forged/mismatched readiness reject. Original command-binding wrapper failure is preserved; the corrected wrapper distinguishes compiler output from linker input.\n- Sole whole-branch review: 0 Critical / 3 Important / 0 Minor; all three input-authentication findings reproduced RED\u2192GREEN and fixed in one pass. Current cc1plus/selection config and original log are bound before/after; malformed marker forms reject. No rereview/minor polishing.\n- 115 indexed proofs / 26,827,355 bytes; 127 additions, zero base-file changes; clean checkout. Before-review proof remains immutable; later review/fix evidence is separate.\n\nPreserve 4,824 base files, 299 old source pins, 10 original artifacts, main, Draft PRs102\u2013112 and all eight native workflow histories. No main/shared-base update, Cloud/registry publication or consumed request replay. Actual new native/GL/provider/official-model/official-ORT calls0. Native allowance0; inherited strict0/4FAIL; new official result NOT_RUN; Stage7 INCOMPLETE. No new RGB/I420/officialONNX equality, first-divergence, GPU freshness, geometry/optical equivalence or instrumentation-performance result.\n\nReproduce into a NEW directory: `/workspace/.cloud-tools/stage7/first-divergence-cpu-replay/bin/python -B -m scripts.panda_sdk_integration --out output/panda-sdk-next-assessment`. Exit0 means the data assessments finished; the resulting execution status remains BLOCKED. Existing output directories reject.\n\nNext implementation is a new reviewed runtime/SDK resolving the seven paths and safe256/computed-origin closure, then a newly qualified full image and mapped/live/driver/receipt gates before a fresh bounded native canary. This diagnostic PR does not implement those missing suppliers or finish the three requested runtime/scientific tasks.\n\nResults, complete rulings/costs and continuation: docs/STAGE7_PANDA_SDK_INTEGRATION_{RESULT,LEDGER,CONTINUATION}.md. Spec/plan: docs/superpowers/{specs,plans}/2026-11-15-panda-sdk-integration.md. Proof index/selection: docs/evidence/panda-sdk-integration-01/. Exact final HEAD/Draft/CI/body/fresh preservation receipt: output/stage7-panda-sdk-integration-01/final-verification.json.\n\nExact final-HEAD push and pull_request CI: all four jobs pass.\n\n- pull_request: [43679226356](https://github.com/rownlvh8875-coder/big-model-closed-loop-benchmark/actions/runs/43679226356); synthetic-unit 132705993416, onnx-interface-test 132705993588; both success, attempt 1, artifacts 0.\n- push: [43679222035](https://github.com/rownlvh8875-coder/big-model-closed-loop-benchmark/actions/runs/43679222035); synthetic-unit 132705981323, onnx-interface-test 132705981504; both success, attempt 1, artifacts 0.\n\nThe ONNX interface job uses a generated SMALL TEST GRAPH ONLY; it does not run the official large model. Exact HEAD, attempt/job/artifact checks, Draft/body roundtrip and fresh preservation are retained in the external final receipt. No main/shared-base update or Cloud/registry publication.\n",
